{
  "name": "a rubric sweep re-queues the corpus and empties search until it drains",
  "description": "ADR-0007 §Endpoints: 'POST /admin/evaluations/sweep — global re-run for prompt/model change'. When the prompt, the model, or a rubric constant changes, every existing score was produced by a different function and is no longer comparable to a new one.\n\nThe consequence the fixture exists to pin is the interaction with ADR-0005's search gate, 'AND rubric_version = $active'. Bumping the active rubric makes the entire scored population fall OUT of search immediately, and back in only as re-evaluation drains. That is deliberate: a leaderboard mixing v1 and v2 scores ranks people by which version happened to judge them. Half-swept results are worse than none, so the sweep is enqueue-only and idempotent — a second call while one is running adds nothing.",
  "seed": ["principals", "catalogue", "repositories", "scored_population"],
  "steps": [
    {
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/search?skills=go"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "_note": "Baseline under rubric v1 — the same two results the discovery case pins.",
        "body": {
          "total": 2,
          "inactive_hidden": 0,
          "ranked_by": "skill:go",
          "page": 1,
          "per_page": 20,
          "results": [
            {
              "id": "<uuid>",
              "display_name": "Alice Okafor",
              "github_login": "aliceok",
              "active": true,
              "skills": [
                {
                  "slug": "go",
                  "standing": "primary",
                  "score": 64.2,
                  "rank": 1
                }
              ],
              "overall_score": 64.2,
              "generalist_score": 64.2,
              "rank": 1,
              "availability": {
                "status": "<string>",
                "expires_at": "<timestamp>"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "<uuid>",
              "display_name": "Bob Nakamura",
              "github_login": "bobn",
              "active": true,
              "skills": [
                {
                  "slug": "go",
                  "standing": "primary",
                  "score": 55.0,
                  "rank": 2
                }
              ],
              "overall_score": 60.4,
              "generalist_score": 122.7,
              "rank": 2,
              "availability": {
                "status": "<string>",
                "expires_at": "<timestamp>"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "Only an admin can sweep. It costs a model call per claim in the corpus.",
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/admin/evaluations/sweep",
        "body": {
          "rubric_version": "v2",
          "reason": "Prompt revision."
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 403,
        "body": {
          "error": "admin_required"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "alice",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/admin/evaluations/sweep",
        "body": {
          "rubric_version": "v2",
          "reason": "Trying it on."
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 403,
        "body": {
          "error": "admin_required"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "A sweep to the CURRENT version is refused. It would re-spend the entire corpus to produce identical numbers.",
      "as": "root",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/admin/evaluations/sweep",
        "body": {
          "rubric_version": "v1",
          "reason": "No-op."
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 422,
        "body": {
          "error": "rubric_version_unchanged",
          "active_rubric_version": "v1"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "root",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/admin/evaluations/sweep",
        "body": {
          "rubric_version": "v99",
          "reason": "Typo."
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 422,
        "_note": "The version must already be loaded from config (ADR-0006). A sweep cannot invent one.",
        "body": {
          "error": "unknown_rubric_version",
          "provided": "v99"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "root",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/admin/evaluations/sweep",
        "body": {
          "rubric_version": "v2",
          "reason": "Conversation-quality weight raised from 0.20 to 0.25."
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 202,
        "_note": "Enqueue only. The endpoint returns as soon as the jobs are written; nothing is judged synchronously.",
        "body": {
          "id": "<uuid>",
          "from_rubric_version": "v1",
          "to_rubric_version": "v2",
          "reason": "Conversation-quality weight raised from 0.20 to 0.25.",
          "claims_enqueued": 1,
          "requested_by": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d001",
          "created_at": "<timestamp>"
        },
        "db": {
          "evaluation_jobs": {
            "where": {
              "status": "pending"
            },
            "count": 1
          },
          "claims": {
            "_note": "Every previously evaluated claim goes back to queued. Withdrawn claims are not swept — there is nothing to rank.",
            "where": {
              "status": "queued"
            },
            "count": 1
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "THE CONSEQUENCE. The active rubric is now v2 and no score has been produced under it, so search is empty.",
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/search?skills=go"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "_note": "Not an error, and not stale v1 rows. An empty result is the honest answer while the corpus is mid-migration.",
        "body": {
          "total": 0,
          "inactive_hidden": 0,
          "ranked_by": "skill:go",
          "page": 1,
          "per_page": 20,
          "results": []
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/leaderboard?kind=overall"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "kind": "overall",
          "rubric_version": "v2",
          "entries": []
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "The contributor's own view is NOT emptied. They keep seeing their standing, marked stale, because it is their own record rather than a ranking.",
      "as": "alice",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/me/skills"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "skills": [
            {
              "slug": "go",
              "standing": "primary",
              "distinct_pr_count": 5,
              "score": 64.2,
              "rubric_version": "v1",
              "stale": true
            }
          ],
          "overall_score": 64.2,
          "generalist_score": 64.2,
          "rubric_version": "v1",
          "stale": true,
          "reevaluation_in_progress": true
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "A second sweep while one is in flight adds nothing. Idempotent by design — a double-click must not double the bill.",
      "as": "root",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/admin/evaluations/sweep",
        "body": {
          "rubric_version": "v2",
          "reason": "Double click."
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 409,
        "body": {
          "error": "sweep_in_progress",
          "id": "<uuid>",
          "claims_remaining": 1
        },
        "db": {
          "evaluation_jobs": {
            "where": {
              "status": "pending"
            },
            "count": 1
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "Drain. Every claim is re-judged under v2 — conversation_quality now carries more weight.",
      "as": "system",
      "request": {
        "method": "RUN_EVALUATOR",
        "path": "/"
      },
      "fake": {
        "ai": {
          "replay_previous_judgements": true
        },
        "rubric": {
          "version": "v2",
          "weights": {
            "conversation_quality": 0.25,
            "craft": 0.1
          }
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "processed": 1,
          "failed": 0
        },
        "db": {
          "claims": {
            "where": {
              "status": "evaluated"
            },
            "count": 1
          },
          "score_snapshots": {
            "_note": "v1 snapshots are retained. A sweep supersedes scores; it does not erase the history of what was once true.",
            "where": {
              "rubric_version": "v1"
            },
            "count": 8
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "Search repopulates under v2. Same people, new numbers, and the order can differ — which is exactly why a half-swept corpus must not be searchable.",
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/search?skills=go"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "total": 2,
          "inactive_hidden": 0,
          "ranked_by": "skill:go",
          "page": 1,
          "per_page": 20,
          "results": [
            {
              "id": "<uuid>",
              "display_name": "Alice Okafor",
              "github_login": "aliceok",
              "active": true,
              "skills": [
                {
                  "slug": "go",
                  "standing": "primary",
                  "score": 60.19,
                  "rank": 1
                }
              ],
              "overall_score": 60.19,
              "generalist_score": 60.19,
              "rank": 1,
              "availability": {
                "status": "<string>",
                "expires_at": "<timestamp>"
              },
              "_note": "Recomputed, not carried over. The seeded standing of 64.2 was written by hand and is not what its own per-PR scores produce: PRComponent over the five seeded scores times 0.85 is 60.19 (ADR-0005). The sweep re-derives it, so this is the first read that shows the evidence's real value."
            },
            {
              "id": "<uuid>",
              "display_name": "Bob Nakamura",
              "github_login": "bobn",
              "active": true,
              "skills": [
                {
                  "slug": "go",
                  "standing": "primary",
                  "score": 55.0,
                  "rank": 2
                }
              ],
              "overall_score": 60.4,
              "generalist_score": 122.7,
              "rank": 2,
              "availability": {
                "status": "<string>",
                "expires_at": "<timestamp>"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "Standing is unchanged by a sweep. Re-judging the same evidence cannot alter how many distinct PRs there are.",
      "as": "alice",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/me/skills"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "skills": [
            {
              "slug": "go",
              "standing": "primary",
              "distinct_pr_count": 5,
              "score": 60.19,
              "rubric_version": "v2",
              "stale": false,
              "promoted_at": "<timestamp>"
            }
          ],
          "overall_score": 60.19,
          "generalist_score": 60.19,
          "rubric_version": "v2",
          "_note": "Recomputed, not carried over. The seeded standing of 64.2 was written by hand and is not what its own per-PR scores produce: PRComponent over the five seeded scores times 0.85 is 60.19 (ADR-0005). The sweep re-derives it, so this is the first read that shows the evidence's real value."
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "With the sweep drained, a new one is permitted again.",
      "as": "root",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/admin/evaluations/sweep",
        "body": {
          "rubric_version": "v1",
          "reason": "Rolling back."
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 202,
        "_note": "Rollback is an ordinary sweep in the other direction. Nothing about the mechanism assumes versions only move forward.",
        "body": {
          "id": "<uuid>",
          "from_rubric_version": "v2",
          "to_rubric_version": "v1",
          "reason": "Rolling back.",
          "claims_enqueued": 1,
          "requested_by": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d001",
          "created_at": "<timestamp>"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
